  "notes": "{雇用|こよう} is a key term in labor and economic discussions, referring to the act of hiring or the state of employment.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {雇用|こよう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to employ, to hire\n- {雇用|こよう}⟦{契約|けいやく}→契約：02698_keiyaku⟧: employment contract\n- {雇用|こよう}⟦{保険|ほけん}→保険：01509_hoken⟧: employment insurance\n- {雇用|こよう}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{創出|そうしゅつ}する→創出する：noentry⟧: to create employment\n\nEMPLOYMENT TYPES IN JAPAN:\n- ⟦{正規|せいき}→正規：03776_seiki⟧{雇用|こよう}: regular employment (full-time, permanent)\n- ⟦{非正規|ひせいき}→非正規：26236_hiseiki⟧{雇用|こよう}: non-regular employment (part-time, contract, temp)\n- ⟦{終身|しゅうしん}→終身：09947_shuushin⟧{雇用|こよう}: lifetime employment (traditional Japanese system, declining)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapan's traditional ⟦{終身|しゅうしん}→終身：09947_shuushin⟧{雇用|こよう} system — where employees stay with one company for their entire career — has been weakening. The rise of ⟦{非正規|ひせいき}→非正規：26236_hiseiki⟧{雇用|こよう} is a major social issue.",
